Subject: notifications: rename local `transient`, a reserved word for Qt 6.10's QML parser

Omarchy v4.0.3 targets a newer Quickshell than Debian ships (0.3.1 vs 0.3.0).
Against Debian's build, `shell/plugins/notifications/Service.qml` fails to parse:

    WARN qml: service plugin load failed for omarchy.notifications:
    .../notifications/Service.qml:149 Expected token `identifier'

Line 149 declares `var transient`, and `transient` is a future-reserved word in
the QML JavaScript grammar this Qt builds against. The whole notifications
service then fails to load, so the shell registers no notification daemon:
`notify-send` fails, and every omarchy script that reports through
`omarchy-notification-send` errors with

    Call failed: Process org.freedesktop.Notifications exited with status 1

Renaming the local variable fixes it. The hints KEY "transient" is a string and
is deliberately left alone — only the identifier is renamed.

Re-check after any Omarchy or Quickshell upgrade: if Debian ships Quickshell
0.3.1+ this patch may become unnecessary, and `patch` will say so.
---
--- a/shell/plugins/notifications/Service.qml
+++ b/shell/plugins/notifications/Service.qml
@@ -146,11 +146,11 @@
   // screen; the distinction only decides whether a DND-silenced one is worth
   // recording at all.
   function isEphemeral(notification) {
-    var transient = false
+    var isTransient = false
     try {
-      transient = !!(notification.hints && notification.hints["transient"])
-    } catch (e) { transient = false }
-    return transient || NotificationLogic.isEphemeralApp(String(notification.appName || ""))
+      isTransient = !!(notification.hints && notification.hints["transient"])
+    } catch (e) { isTransient = false }
+    return isTransient || NotificationLogic.isEphemeralApp(String(notification.appName || ""))
   }
 
   function handleNotification(notification) {
